{{!-- Primitive 5 — the toggle. A pill and a knob in the two inks: the track is faint ink off and
      full ink on, the knob is paper either way and slides the difference. This is the system's
      only on/off control — a square box is core's furniture and says nothing this does not.

      The checkbox itself stays in the form, because it is what `FormDataExtended` reads; it is
      only taken out of the visual order, so `name`, `checked` and `disabled` behave exactly as
      they would on a bare input. Pass `id` when a label elsewhere in the row points at it.

      `action` makes it a control instead of a form field — the switch then reports to the
      application's actions map on click and carries no `name`. It goes on the INPUT, never on the
      surrounding `<label>`: a label forwards a click to its input, so a `data-action` on the label
      would match the label's own click and again on the forwarded one, and the toggle would fire
      twice and land back where it started. The handler reads whatever the row it sits on names.

      `tooltip` goes on the LABEL, for the mirror reason: core raises a tooltip from the dataset of
      the element the pointer ENTERS (`TooltipManager##onActivate` reads `event.target.dataset`
      and nothing above it), and the input is a 1px square nobody's pointer ever enters. On the
      label it covers the whole pill. `aria-label` stays on the input, which is what a screen
      reader focuses.

      `tooltip` is the word the switch would carry if it had a label — it has none by design, so
      the row's own reading is where it goes. --}}
<label class="cairn-switch"{{#if tooltip}} data-tooltip-text="{{tooltip}}"{{/if}}>
    <input type="checkbox" {{#if id}}id="{{id}}" {{/if}}{{#if field}}name="{{field}}" {{/if}}
           {{#if action}}data-action="{{action}}" {{/if}}
           {{#if tooltip}}aria-label="{{tooltip}}" {{/if}}
           {{checked value}} {{disabled disabled}} />
    <span class="cairn-switch-track"><span class="cairn-switch-knob"></span></span>
</label>
